    {
      "id": "claim_d24e09e945f148e795da34ecbc1d54ea",
      "statement": "The identity — and therefore the release, the environment and the framework swap — is resolved once lazily on first use of Observability.identity, while the caller's module name is captured eagerly at Observability construction because from a request the stack would name the host (Odoo) instead of the library that built the bus.",
